### 5.2 Model Descriptions

| Model                         | Table Name                     | Purpose                                                                                    |
|-------------------------------|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `User`                        | `users`                        | Application user with local auth (password, OTP, reset token) and Google OAuth linking.    |
| `Dataset`                     | `datasets`                     | Logical dataset catalog entry owned by a user. Supports soft-delete via `is_deleted` flag. |
| `Folder`                      | `folders`                      | Virtual folder hierarchy (self-referential tree via `parent_id`). Per-user, per-name unique within parent. |
| `UploadedFile`                | `uploaded_files`               | Physical file record with disk path, size, and SHA-256 `master_hash` (globally unique).    |
| `DatasetFolderFilesMapping`   | `dataset_folder_files_mapping` | Junction table linking a dataset, an optional folder, and a file to a user. Enables many-to-many relationships and deduplication. |

### 5.3 Key Relationships

- **User → Dataset**: One-to-Many. A user can own multiple datasets.
- **User → Folder**: One-to-Many. A user can create multiple folders.
- **Folder → Folder**: Self-referential One-to-Many (parent-child tree).
- **Dataset ↔ UploadedFile**: Many-to-Many through `DatasetFolderFilesMapping`. A single physical file can be linked to multiple datasets.
- **Folder ↔ UploadedFile**: Many-to-Many through `DatasetFolderFilesMapping`. Files are placed in folders via the mapping.
- **UploadedFile** is globally unique by `master_hash` — this enables deduplication across users and datasets.

### 5.4 Redis Data Structures

| Key Pattern                      | Type         | Purpose                                                        | TTL                          |
|----------------------------------|--------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------|
| `user:sessions:{user_id}`       | Sorted Set   | Active session tracking (members: `sid`, scores: timestamps)   | `REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS`  |
| `upload:{upload_id}:meta`       | Hash         | Upload session metadata (user_id, filename, filesize, etc.)    | `UPLOAD_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS` |
| `upload:{upload_id}:bitmap`     | Bitmap       | Bit-per-chunk received tracking                                | `UPLOAD_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS` |
| `upload:{upload_id}:chunk_hashes`| Hash        | Per-chunk SHA-256 hashes (field: chunk_index, value: hash)     | `UPLOAD_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS` |

### 5.5 Filesystem Layout

```
uploads/
├── .parts/                          # Temporary chunk storage
│   └── {upload_id}/                 # Per-session directory
│       ├── 000000.part              # Chunk 0
│       ├── 000001.part              # Chunk 1
│       └── ...
└── files/                           # Final assembled files
    ├── report.csv
    ├── data.json
    └── ...
```

