### Confirmed Dataset Lifecycle Flow (Test-Verified)

```
POST /v1/datasets  →  create_dataset()
  │  Uniqueness: case-insensitive name check per user (func.lower)
  │  Initial status: always "Created"
  └→ DatasetResponse {id, name, status="Created", file_count=0, tree=null}

GET /v1/datasets  →  get_datasets()
  │  Filters: is_deleted=False, user_id match
  │  Respects: page, limit, include_completed
  └→ list[DatasetResponse]

GET /v1/datasets/{id}  →  get_dataset_by_id() + get_dataset_tree_for_dataset()
  │  Ownership check: 403 if user_id mismatch
  │  Not found: 404 if is_deleted=True or non-existent
  └→ DatasetResponse {... tree: UploadsTreeResponse}

PATCH /v1/datasets/{id}  →  update_dataset()
  │  Status transitions (allowed):
  │    Created → Draft or Completed
  │    Draft   → Completed
  │    Completed → (no transitions, raises 400)
  │  Name: case-insensitive uniqueness, no-op if same name
  └→ DatasetResponse

DELETE /v1/datasets/{id}  →  delete_dataset()
  │  NOTE: HARD DELETE (not soft-delete via is_deleted flag)
  │  Cascades: deletes all DatasetFolderFilesMapping rows
  │  Cascades: deletes referenced UploadedFile physical file rows
  └→ {status: "deleted", dataset_id: "..."}

POST /v1/datasets/{id}/files  →  attach_file_to_dataset()
  │  IDOR guard: user must own ≥1 mapping to file_id
  │    → 404 if file does not exist at all
  │    → 403 if file exists but user has no mapping to it
  │  Status guard: 400 if dataset.status == "Completed"
  │  Folder resolution: _get_folder_tree(relative_path) if provided
  │  Idempotent: existing mapping not duplicated
  └→ DatasetAttachFileResponse {status="attached", dataset_id, file_id, folder_id}
```

### Confirmed Virtual Folder Tree Flow (Test-Verified)

```
_get_folder_tree(db, user, relative_path, filename)
  │  None / "" path → returns None (file stored at dataset root)
  │  "a/b/c" path → creates folders a → b → c (parent chain)
  │  Idempotent: queries by (user_id, parent_id, name) before inserting
  │  _validate_relative_path():
  │    "/" prefix → HTTP 400
  │    ".." segments → HTTP 400
  │    Empty/None → []
  │  _resolve_folder_parts():
  │    Strips trailing segment if it matches filename
  └→ Folder (leaf node) or None
```

### Key Architectural Findings

| Finding | Detail |
|---------|--------|
| `DELETE /v1/datasets/{id}` is a **hard delete** | Removes the `Dataset` row from the DB entirely. The `is_deleted` flag on the model is for filtering (e.g., `get_datasets` hides `is_deleted=True`), but `delete_dataset()` calls `db.delete(dataset)` — not a soft flag. |
| IDOR guard is **service-layer enforced** | `attach_file_to_dataset()` queries `DatasetFolderFilesMapping` by `user_id` to verify ownership — not relying on route-level auth alone. |
| Status sync is **triggered on every file add/remove** | `_sync_dataset_status_from_mappings()` is called after any mapping change. It upgrades `Created`→`Draft` (≥1 file) or downgrades `Draft`→`Created` (0 files). `Completed` is never touched by the sync. |
| `pg_insert ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` is PostgreSQL-only | `finalize_upload()` uses `from sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import insert as pg_insert` which will raise `CompileError` on SQLite. This is **resolved in test isolation** by patching `file_services.pg_insert` with a SQLite-compatible `sa_insert(table)` wrapper whose `on_conflict_do_nothing()` is a no-op. No production code changes required. |

