### External FTP Pull Ingestion Gatekeeper Flow (v3.3 Component 1)

```
1. Client sends connect request:
    ├─ POST /v1/ingest/ftp/connect
    ├─ JSON: { host, port, username, password, duration_seconds, until_i_stop, graceful_expiry, allow_insecure }
    └─ Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

2. Gatekeeper validation sequence:
    ├─ _resolve_current_user() → validates JWT Bearer token
    ├─ _check_rate_limit(user_id)
    │   ├─ Redis INCR ext_ftp:rate:{user_id} (Window: 300s, Max: 5 attempts)
    │   └─ If count > 5 → raises 429 FtpRateLimitError
    ├─ _probe_ftp_connection(host, port, username, password, allow_insecure)
    │   ├─ ftplib.FTP_TLS probe (timeout=10s)
    │   ├─ connect() → auth() → prot_p() → login() → quit()
    │   ├─ If TLS fails & allow_insecure=True → fallback ftplib.FTP login
    │   └─ Errors: 400 (TLS rejected), 401 (Auth failed), 504 (Unreachable host)
    ├─ fernet_encrypt(password) → Fernet (AES-256) token using FERNET_KEY
    └─ _store_ftp_credentials(user_id, payload)
        └─ SET ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} (ex=1800s idle TTL)

3. Client sends disconnect request:
    ├─ POST /v1/ingest/ftp/disconnect?force=false (or force=true)
    ├─ Body (if force=true): { delete_completed_files: boolean }
    └─ Headers: Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

4. Stateful disconnect execution:
    ├─ If force == false (Normal Draining):
    │   ├─ Check _count_active_ftp_jobs(user_id) in AsyncIngestionJob
    │   ├─ If 0 active jobs → delete Redis key ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} → 200 OK
    │   └─ If > 0 active jobs → set state="draining" in Redis → 409 Conflict (FtpSessionDrainingError)
    │
    └─ If force == true (Force Nuke):
        ├─ Cancel pending/in_progress AsyncIngestionJob rows for user
        ├─ If delete_completed_files == true:
        │   ├─ Delete DatasetFolderFilesMapping rows for user
        │   ├─ Check SELECT COUNT(*) on DatasetFolderFilesMapping per file_id
        │   └─ If ref_count == 0 → delete physical file + delete UploadedFile row
        └─ Delete Redis key ext_ftp:creds:{user_id} → 200 OK
```


